  "residual_model": {
    "applies_to": "the residual model is exactly v12's (nb feature set, matched rows outside LIRF, weight 1.0, single booster); each candidate then blends the result with ens_v20_bag_q_all at 0.7 on every row outside LIRF (the incumbent's blend), and adds a second blend on the lirf_nonpop_matched scope with one v21 / v22 table: value = (1 - w) * v9 + w * table there (the table REPLACES the incumbent's LIRF blend, it is not stacked on it); every other LIRF row keeps v9 exactly.",
    "blend": "post-hoc convex combination with the extra table adsb_full (candidate_values in tools/run_adsb_v11.py); a NaN learner value leaves the row unblended",
